Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: allow firmware nodes to opt out of auto boot

Some systems expose a remote processor dynamically after userspace has
installed its firmware and runtime dependencies.  Starting it asynchronously
from rproc_add() races those dependencies and can leave an extra power
reference when userspace also requests a start.

Honor an opt-in qcom,no-auto-boot property while keeping every existing
platform descriptor unchanged by default.

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -775,0 +776,2 @@ static int adsp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+	if (of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,no-auto-boot"))
+		rproc->auto_boot = false;
